      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"fjur\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"28300\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/48/4849_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> fjur:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>However, I suppose <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/rabit\">@Rabit</a> <em>did</em> like both posts, which could mean they’re okay . . .</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not really up to us, as we Mods are just community members who help out as volunteers. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> That call is up to actual GTG folks.</p>\n<p>However, since a person can’t play the game without the components, I don’t think they’ll be worried. I mean, the Sentinels rulebook has been available online for years. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
